WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.030
NARRATOR: Pet grooming
combs are specifically

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.470
designed for animal fur.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.720
They can get down to
the roots to detangle,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.430
loosen, and remove dead hair.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.895
A good grooming comb is
essential to the primping

00:00:19.895 --> 00:00:20.695
process.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.990
It's believed that the pets
of British and French nobility

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.870
were the first to be regularly
groomed centuries ago.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.797
Today, a lot of pets
receive the royal treatment.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.830
At this factory, pet
combs start with bundles

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:46.970
of long brass bars.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.995
A computer-guided saw slices
them into 6-inch pieces.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.420
Each piece will be
transformed into a comb body.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:16.300
An employee inserts six of
the brass pieces into a vise

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.335
and tightens the clamps.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:23.770
A computerized drill carves
dimples into the ends

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.580
of each of the blanks.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.660
This is called a pre-drill.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.910
The drill returns
to each dimple,

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:35.100
producing precisely-cut
holes to join

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.360
the combe body to a handle.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:44.840
Next, a computerized drill
bores into the brass pieces,

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.960
creating small holes
for the comb's teeth.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.410
The spacing of the
holes varies depending

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:56.020
on the type of comb being made.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:59.230
Combs with tightly-spaced
teeth are used for finer fir.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.510
The combs are now
ready for teeth.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:08.280
An employee inserts three
comb bodies in a fixture,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.919
then grabs a handful
of steel pins

00:02:10.919 --> 00:02:13.130
and pops them into
the holes one by one.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.410
These steel teeth aren't sharp.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:21.030
They've been blunted
to avoid hurting

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.320
the animal during combing.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.610
She gently taps the
steel teeth with a hammer

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.260
to force them further
into the holes.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.290
She brushes off any
residual shavings

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.400
from the earlier drilling.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.520
Then she places the
combs on a demagnetizer.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.640
It erases any magnetic
fields in the steel teeth

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.470
that could compromise
the chrome plating

00:02:49.470 --> 00:02:50.625
finish they will soon receive.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.725
Next, a punch sets the steel
teeth in their final position.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.760
At another station, a
device cuts extruded

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.110
aluminum into shorter pieces.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.735
These pieces of aluminum
will be the pet comb handles.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.390
Their contoured shape is
designed for easy gripping.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.170
A worker clamps one of
the handles in a fixture.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.150
It holds the handle
steady as he drills

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.365
rivet holes in both ends.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.000
The fixture also helps
locate the holes through line

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.050
channels called bushings.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.980
By drilling through
the bushings,

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.530
he produces accurate
rivet holes every time.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:53.120
In the meantime,
the comb assembly

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.190
has been plated with a
rust-resistant nickel

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:56.060
and chrome finish.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.800
It's ready to be
joined to the handle.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.430
An employee aligns
the holes in the comb

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:06.340
with the holes in the handle
and places them in a riveter.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.520
The tool flattens the
rivets against the handle

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.320
on both sides.

00:04:17.149 --> 00:04:22.920
Then she dabs adhesive around
the open ends of the handle

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:24.480
and inserts plastic caps.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.910
She hammers the caps down.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.490
The glue sets quickly,
creating a strong seal.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.830
After about a half hour of
work, this pet grooming comb

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.450
is now complete.

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:52.150
It should last for many years.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.090
There will no doubt
be many tangles ahead.

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:56.950
But this comb will
pull through them.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:01.410
And in the end, Fido will look
and feel a whole lot better.

